Z||000000||fropuff||08-06-2000||10:38 PM||||Hey, I just did one stupid-a$$ thing.  For those of you who are as dumb as me, don't try pounding on the tail light assembly to fix your flickering turn signal.  Hit it the wrong way; busted the plastic cover.  It really pisses me off that I could be so stupid.  Now, for my question:  Do I need to get a new assembly, or does the cover come off?  I just need the plastic cover.  The rest of the assembly is in perfect condition.  I just hope that I don't have to shell out $150 to get a new assembly.  Please help!  Thanks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||08-06-2000||11:11 PM||||The lens cover comes off!!!! Your ok, Post in the mall and I'm sure one of the members will have some.  You might say there glued on.... it's some kind of black weather sealer strip that holds them together, Take your time prying them apart!!!! some of them are tight, but they do come apart.<P><BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
Z||000002||fropuff||08-06-2000||11:14 PM||||That's good to hear.  Went on the Fiero Store site.  $127.00 for a COVER!  I don't even want to know what the assembly is.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||08-07-2000||02:44 AM||||You should try a boneyard to, theres usually at least one good side lens.<BR>As far as the Fiero Store and some of these other "fiero specialty places" go, they can kiss my a$$!! I have bought a couple of things from the Fiero Store, but that was when I knew little about Fieros...when I just started getting into them.<BR>I dont know what in the hell the fiero store was thinking when they made their prices! Pu-leez!! While Im at it, Im gonna bash another..Kick Hill. Well, I wont, but take a look at their prices for USED parts! Come on, there Fieros, not Dusenburgs (spell?)...I have to laugh when I see prices for some of these thing...100 bucks for a front fender, I can go to the bonyard and get one for 5 bucks!<BR>Anyway, enough ranting and raving....what were we talking about again?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
